{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_0fb1c9eb50114bc2bd6ee169","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /home/phaedrus/development/misty-step/canopy/.forest/worktrees/1788551444310324575-fixer && for full in 0f61b4007878a9bd93ad014a750221fbcb5aff62 c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a ca9e23795abebbe11ec519332a79b9c1d96d9ae2 e15fcacd647bb54155c7056356bf34e2238497e6 fbb9338e93e8b83963ed35a6fa287adb2fc8e5c6; do\n  oid=$(git rev-parse \"refs/forest/v1/verdict/$full\")\n  echo \"=== $full ===\"\n  git show \"$oid\":verdict.json\n  echo\ndone"},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== 0f61b4007878a9bd93ad014a750221fbcb5aff62 ===\n{\"schema\":\"forest.verdict.v1\",\"revision\":\"0f61b4007878a9bd93ad014a750221fbcb5aff62\",\"verdict\":\"approve\",\"summary\":\"Checks test (go test ./...) and vet (go vet ./...) both pass with exit 0. The Revision gates the fleet and instance HTMX polling triggers with [document.hidden === false], so background polls are skipped while the tab is hidden and resume when visible; the vendored HTMX 2.0.9 parser/evaluator confirms the filter cancels poll issuance when the expression is not true and still reschedules the next tick. templates_test.go verifies both rendered triggers contain the visibility gate. Fast-forward from origin/master fbb9338 is verified; no blocking findings.\",\"time\":\"2026-09-04T18:45:43Z\"}\n\n=== c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a ===\n{\"schema\": \"forest.verdict.v1\", \"revision\": \"c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a\", \"verdict\": \"approve\", \"summary\": \"Checks passed (go test ./... and go vet ./...). Test-only revision adds coverage for audit divergence stale override rendering: divergent pass/trusted render class stale with the result text, while equal or missing revision pairs retain the ok class. Verified against auditView in view.go and by running the new subtests; revision is one commit ahead of origin/master and fast-forwards cleanly.\", \"time\": \"2026-09-04T19:28:49Z\"}\n\n=== ca9e23795abebbe11ec519332a79b9c1d96d9ae2 ===\n{\"schema\":\"forest.verdict.v1\",\"revision\":\"ca9e23795abebbe11ec519332a79b9c1d96d9ae2\",\"verdict\":\"approve\",\"summary\":\"Checks test and vet pass with exit 0. Revision ca9e2379 is a fast-forward of origin/master (d570c11). Diff changes discovery.go and discovery_test.go: scanDevelopmentRoot now recognizes forest.yaml-declared checkouts in addition to legacy .forest+executable forest checkouts, and resolves the Forest binary as repo-local, then PATH, then parent/iron-forest/forest. New tests cover forest.yaml discovery, non-executable local fallback to factory, and PATH preference. No blocking correctness, security, or maintainability findings.\",\"time\":\"2026-09-04T19:01:18Z\"}\n\n=== e15fcacd647bb54155c7056356bf34e2238497e6 ===\n{\"schema\":\"forest.verdict.v1\",\"revision\":\"e15fcacd647bb54155c7056356bf34e2238497e6\",\"verdict\":\"approve\",\"summary\":\"Test-only refactor: extract scanDevelopmentRoot from scanDevelopmentRoots and replace the host-dependent TestDiscoverLocalInstances with a deterministic mocked-checkout test. Production discovery behavior is unchanged; go test and go vet pass; Revision fast-forwards origin/master.\",\"time\":\"2026-09-04T17:54:59Z\"}\n\n=== fbb9338e93e8b83963ed35a6fa287adb2fc8e5c6 ===\n{\"schema\":\"forest.verdict.v1\",\"revision\":\"fbb9338e93e8b83963ed35a6fa287adb2fc8e5c6\",\"verdict\":\"approve\",\"summary\":\"Checks test and vet pass (exit 0). Revision fast-forwards origin/master e15fcacd. Diff preserves explicit inventory during discovery reconciliation (app.go App.discovered) and gives startup-discovered instances exactly one worker (instanceWorker.started); added tests cover single-worker startup, worker cleanup after prune, and explicit retention. go test -race also passes. No blocking findings.\",\"time\":\"2026-09-04T18:28:42Z\"}\n\n"}],"details":{}}}
